      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Three patients of ischemic heart disease associated with protein C deficiency are reported. Although delayed diagnosis of protein C deficiency resulted in the failure of repeated interventions, coronary artery bypass grafting performed after making the correct diagnosis has led to satisfactory mid-term results under strict anticoagulation therapy. The level of protein C should be measured more frequently in the field of ischemic heart disease and earlier diagnosis of its deficiency should be made, because measurement of protein C does not cost much."},
